# What the Account page says (src/account/view.rs, src/account/vm.rs).
account-page-heading = Your account
account-signed-in-as = Signed in as { $name }
account-loading = Loading your account…
account-signed-out = You are signed out.
account-signed-out-help = Sign in to see and change your account.
account-sign-in-with = Sign in with
account-unavailable = Accounts are not available right now. Everything else in CityLoom still works.
account-sign-out = Sign out
account-linked-heading = Linked sign-ins
account-linked-note = You can sign in with any of these.
account-identity = { $provider } ({ $label })
account-identity-bare = { $provider }
account-unlink = Unlink
account-unlink-named = Unlink { $what }
account-unlinked = Sign-in unlinked.
account-only-one = This is your only sign-in, so it cannot be unlinked.
account-link-heading = Link another sign-in
account-link-with = Link { $provider }
account-link-note = You can also link a second account from a provider you already use; the labels tell them apart.
account-storage-heading = Where is your work kept?
account-storage-lead = Choose one. You can change it later on this page.
account-storage-device = Keep my work on this device only
account-storage-device-help = This choice is recorded. Your work stays on this device, and nothing you make is sent to the server. If your work was stored on the server, that copy is deleted.
account-storage-server = Store my work on the server
account-storage-server-help = Your work stays in this browser and is copied to the server, so every device you sign in on gets it. Work already in this browser, including work made while signed out or by someone else who used it, is merged into your account.
account-storage-set-device = Your choice is recorded: keep your work on this device only. The copy on the server was deleted.
account-storage-set-server = Your choice is recorded: store your work on the server.
account-stop-heading = Stop storing your work on the server?
account-stop-warning = This deletes your work from the server and keeps the copy in this browser. Your other devices keep their own copies but stop syncing.
account-stop-yes = Delete the server copy
account-stop-no = Keep storing my work
account-privacy-heading = What is stored about you
account-privacy-sealed = Encrypted on the server with a key of your own: your name and sign-ins and, if you store your work there, the places you edited, your area rules and the area you chose.
account-privacy-plain = Not encrypted, because the server matches and sorts on them: the OpenStreetMap ids of the places you edited, the ids of your rules and the time of each edit.
account-privacy-delete = Deleting your account deletes all of it from the server.
account-delete-heading = Delete your account
account-delete = Delete account…
account-delete-confirm-heading = Delete your account?
account-delete-warning = This removes your account, your linked sign-ins and everything stored under them from the server at once, including the work you stored there. Copies in the server’s backups are removed when those backups expire, according to Railway’s retention period. Work kept on this device is not affected.
account-delete-yes = Delete my account
account-delete-no = Keep my account
account-deleted = Your account was deleted.
account-failed = That did not work. Try again.
